    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1956-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Combining the fractional terms, \\[ \\begin{gathered} -\\frac1{1+\\sqrt3}+\\frac1{1-\\sqrt3} \\\\ =\\frac{(1+\\sqrt3)-(1-\\sqrt3)} {(1+\\sqrt3)(1-\\sqrt3)}\\\\ =\\frac{2\\sqrt3}{-2}\\\\ =-\\sqrt3. \\end{gathered} \\] Adding the initial \\(1\\) gives \\(1-\\sqrt3.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the two fractional terms over \\((1+\\sqrt3)(1-\\sqrt3)\\)",
        "The product of the conjugate denominators is \\(1-3=-2\\)"
      ],
